<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;
Thanks for the reply. The reason I used regular expressions was that the actual XML is contained within a log file that contains other information besides xml.  Will the XML:LibXML handle any type of file or does it strictly need a xml file?
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;  I tried the following using this script and am getting a parser error Start tag expected, '&lt;' not found.  Below is the code:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;code&gt;
#!/usr/bin/perl
use XML::LibXML;
my $requestId = $ARGV[0];
my $fileName = "sample.xml";

print "$requestId\n";
print "$fileName\n";

my $doc = XML::LibXML-&gt;load_xml(string=&gt;$fileName);
my @nodes = $doc-&gt;findnodes("/*/EventInfo[\@RequestId='$requestId']");
for my $node (@nodes) {
  print "### ", $node-&gt;getParentNode-&gt;toString, " ###\n\n";
}
&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
